---
import { stockwellReview, muncieReview, importedSourceInventory, recentRecordTargets } from '../data/recent-family-review';
import { familyMapAncestryById } from '../data/family-map';
import { upbringing } from '../data/close-family-evidence';
const branches=[{name:'Stockwell biological branch and Gloria’s family',rows:stockwellReview},{name:'Muncie family that raised Patrick',rows:muncieReview}];
---
<section id="recent-family-review" class="recent-family-review" aria-labelledby="recent-family-heading">
  <span class="editorial-kicker">Close family · evidence audit · 6 October 2026</span>
  <h2 id="recent-family-heading">Strengthening the first five generations</h2>
  <p>Counting parents as generation 1, grandparents as 2, through great-great-great-grandparents as 5. All 31 paternal positions have names recorded. A filled position is a family assertion, not a proved relationship. The Muncie upbringing branch is reviewed alongside it.</p>
  <p><strong>Mark is Patrick’s biological father. Fred Richard Muncie raised Patrick.</strong> This is Tom’s family testimony, recorded 6 October 2026; legal adoption is not inferred. <a href="#patrick-biological-and-raised-family">Tom’s testimony ↗</a></p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#mark-marker-dates">Mark’s photographed marker corroborates his recorded birth and death dates.</a> The inspected 1950 census places him with William R. and Dorothy D. Stockwell; biological paternity remains unresolved.</li>
    <li><a href="#muncie-close-household-1940">The inspected 1940 census names Emma, her son Fred, daughter-in-law Mae and grandson Fred Richard.</a> Mae Etling’s original 1938 marriage now names parents for both spouses. Fred Richard’s direct birth-parent record remains pending.</li>
    <li><a href="#brown-original-parent-conflict">Hines Brown’s death certificate and application index name Lacy as mother, contradicting Mary Lamb.</a> The imported parent line remains flagged for review.</li>
    <li><a href="#luneta-recorded-parents">Luneta’s parents are now Earl B. Etling and Blanche B. Taladay (Belle) in the research map.</a> Their 1920 marriage supplies four fifth-generation parent names. Her birth year remains disputed.</li>
  </ul>
  {branches.map(branch=><details class="family-fallback"><summary>{branch.name} · {branch.rows.length} named positions reviewed</summary>
    <p>Collection references below are the imported source inventory. Repeated references to the same collection are counted once; none of these counts means the underlying documents were inspected or the person’s parentage was proved.</p>
    <div class="recent-audit-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Generation</th><th>Person &amp; recorded dates</th><th>Source leads &amp; relationship review</th></tr></thead><tbody>{branch.rows.map(row=>{
      const p=familyMapAncestryById[row.id], inventory=importedSourceInventory(row.id);
      return <tr><td>{row.generation}</td><td><a href={`/family/?focus=${p.id}`}>{p.name}</a><small>{p.dates}</small></td><td>
        {row.id===upbringing.child?'Mark → Patrick: user-confirmed biological father; original birth record pending.':row.id==='p002'?'Emma → Fred Victor: son named in inspected 1940 census.':row.id===upbringing.biologicalFather?'1950: son in William and Dorothy Stockwell household. Biological father unresolved; see new evidence.':row.id==='mft-e562d673-0941-4d90-82d4-c747c5db6db3'?'Contradicted: death certificate and application index name Lacy; imported maternity remains under review.':row.id==='mft-0409914c-16fd-4485-baaa-31083b6a4b01'?'Parents corroborated by 1938 marriage, 1930 census and own application index; birth year disputed.':row.id==='p001'?'Palmiero / Paul → Fred: probable match from original marriage and county alias certificate.':["p024","p025"].includes(p.id)?'Named in daughter’s marriage and application; own parents named in 1920 marriage. Exact dates under review.':["p026","p027","p028","p029"].includes(p.id)?'Named by the child in the original 1920 marriage; exact identity and dates need earlier records.':p.id===upbringing.raisedBy?'Raised Patrick: user confirmed. Own parentage: probable census household inference.':['p022','p023','p008','p009'].includes(p.id)?'Named in the child’s Ohio death certificate; Italian identity and record matches remain under review.':'Original relationship evidence still needs inspection.'}
        <details><summary>{inventory.collections.length} distinct imported source collections</summary><ul>{inventory.collections.map(c=><li><a href={c.url}>{c.name}</a></li>)}</ul>{!inventory.collections.length&&<p>See the independent research profile and its cited records.</p>}</details>
      </td></tr>;
    })}</tbody></table></div>
  </details>)}
  <details class="family-fallback"><summary>Prioritized records to check next</summary><ol>{recentRecordTargets.map(t=><li><strong>{t.name}.</strong> {t.target}<small>{t.limit}</small></li>)}</ol><p>For generations 4 and 5, compare each child’s birth or marriage record with the named parent household and probate. Names in the imported account stay provisional as proof until those documents are checked; no missing identities or dates are guessed.</p></details>
</section>
